{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455108-tc-part-16-it-s-like-someone-detonated-a-goulash-in-here","id":1455108,"title":"TC part 16: \"It's like someone detonated a goulash in here.\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-18T07:04:21-07:00","id":1455108,"title":"TC part 16: \"It's like someone detonated a goulash in here.\"","content":"The last part is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452636-tc-part-15-worst-timing-ever-covid\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Ah, voice chat growing pains from grown-ass adults who ought to know the pitfalls of voice chat. Last night's game being dominated not by nightly scheming, plots upon plots, and a spot of the good old ultra-violence, but...significant other arguments, pets, mechanical keyboards from people who don't understand push-to-talk, and the like. At least nobody left their mic on while going to the bathroom again.<br /> <br /> By that I mean me. I was the one in our group who once didn't mute before going to take a monster shit. I figured the gain on the mic wasn't that high and I could have my cake and eat it too by roleplaying from the commode, and I was wrong.<br /> <br /> So, not content to make an absolute clusterfuck of the 1413 story, my players weren't done yet. It was only once the players had Ventrue, Tremere, Tzimisce, and a delegation of Ashirra that included a Salubri, that they started questioning the logic of hosting a tournament to promote &quot;unity&quot; among the Siebenburgen. It was also news to them the Ashirra had taken up residence in Brasov, because to the best of their knowledges and various information networks, Brasov was still devoid of any and all Cainite presence having been scoured from top to bottom by the Inquisition.<br /> <br /> It's totally not a prelude to the Ottoman invasion or anything. Also, the PC prince, who I'll remind everyone is a Gangrel currently being possessed by [Tzimisce]...is of Persian descent <i>and a Muslim</i>. So it's not like he has no vested interest in Assamites showing up in the city, totally promising they're just there to meet and greet the new neighbors and don't hold any ill intent or ulterior motive at all, least of all towards the Tremere currently visiting the city.<br /> <br /> Most of the game was the PC's interacting with various Cainites at court. Radu was there with some of his childer, probing for how the PC's felt about the Anarch revolt and sharing some information about how the Ventrue's tactics are changing from overt despotism, to decidedly gentler but more insidious tactics. One of Vencel Rikard's childer -- and a representative of the Holy Roman Ventrue -- was there leading the Ventrue delegation, and the PC's noted the Hungarian and Eastern Lord Ventrue seem to have gotten over their shit and are presenting a united front. The PC's figured out the Ventrue weren't really engaging, or seeming to care to engage, but were quite obviously just casing the joint, something of particular note as they're residing in Nova's former domain meaning the Ventrue would have all the information they needed about seizing the court and deposing the city's Cainites.<br /> <br /> And of course, the Tremere consisted of Alba Iulia's prince, an elder about which they knew precious little, and two they knew well: the bureaucrat who had helped them so much back in 1197 who had originally given the Lasombra PC the Libram Terram before disappearing for two hundred years, and a former Knight of the Black Cross who had been associated with the coterie back when the Ventrue PC was around. What the PC's didn't know (and that I had actually forgotten until later in the game session), were these Tremere were all from a certain, key, lineage that would prove important later.<br /> <br /> Ecaterina was there also, pointing out how the city is a powder keg waiting to blow, and if the PC's know what's best for them, when the fighting starts they'll either keep their heads down or make sure their fangs are in the necks of the elders. They know for a fact Ecaterina is Anarch, and at this point they're still under the belief she's a 1500-year-old, 7th generation, Methuselah (remember, she promotes the falsehood she's Dominic's childe, and was embraced during the Carthage days) who is under zero circumstances someone to be fucked with.<br /> <br /> Last, the Tremere got to the point: the Tremere still owe clan boons to the PC's, regardless of the PC's relations to the clan. They extend an invitation to the PC's to help found the Camarilla with the Tremere as sponsors and mediators between themselves and the Ventrue, as a show of good faith. By this point all the PC's have Clan Enmity (Ventrue), so that's no small offer.<br /> <br /> The PC's retire for the day, and the Lasombra is on the way back to his haven when he is intercepted by Alba Iulia's prince. The Tremere wastes no time telling the PC the Ventrue plan to have their ghouls attack the PC's havens, while using the castle's secret passages to seize it, via their ghouls during the day. The prince tells the PC to consider himself under protection, as the Tremere's sire ordained the Lasombra is under no circumstances to be harmed. The Lasombra PC asks who the Tremere's sire is, and the response is...rather chilling...to say the least: Goratrix.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra was the one who sabotaged the geomantic web, directly causing Goratrix's humiliation and fall after Goratrix had schemed with the coterie to carve alternate runes allowing him to directly tap Kupala's power. So, the Lasombra knows Goratrix still lives, and probably holds a grudge. At this point the coterie's ultimate survival tactic may as well be just to piss off every methuselah they meet, and let the methuselahs keep themselves busy fighting each other for who has the privilege of finally killing the coterie.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra finds somewhere else to sleep.<br /> <br /> The Setite's haven gets attacked during the day, and he only got one round to act. He made it count, killing one of his attackers, but he fell asleep in time for the haven's attackers to try to stake him and drag him out in daylight before his ghouls and cult fought them off. But before then, he ended up crippled with a combination of lethal and aggravated from sunlight. The other two PC's are ancillae Gangrel, so good luck tracking their asses down during the day.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel Prince took it upon himself, knowing what's coming, to replace the court's servants and ghouls with schlacta absolutely armed for bear. And that brings us to what's really going on: I worked this out with the player beforehand. He's being possessed by Tzimisce. His plan was to set the stage for the Anarch revolt in Transylvania, wiping the Siebenburgen's slate clean in a single decapitating strike. The tourney was the most obvious trap in existence, being so insidious in its obviousness: the Tremere and Ventrue being supernaturally compelled to believe they could preempt the trap, taking Mediasch in a single decisive blow of their own before the Anarchs could act. Hence, the daytime raid on the havens of the city's vampires.<br /> <br /> The PC's suspected Ecaterina was influencing the Gangrel PC, when in fact it was the <i>opposite</i>: the Gangrel PC was manipulating <i>Ecaterina</i>, ensuring she and her Brujah would be present in the city to retaliate against the Ventrue and Tremere once they acted. The daytime attacks fail, and it turns out the Tremere fled the city even before daybreak, leaving the Ventrue to their fate...because I realized every last Tremere PC I brought there, <i>somehow</i>, was a member of House Goratrix. The Ventrue attempt to flee, but retribution is swift and brutal, and all are killed by a combination of Brujah and the other Gangrel PC.<br /> <br /> Which leaves one final act to ignite the Anarch revolt in Transylvania: Radu brings the Lasombra PC a request from Dragomir Basarab, who suspects Tzimisce Anarchs are on the precipice of finding and diablerizing [Tzimisce], and wants the PC's help stopping it. The Lasombra's player found this odd and questioned it OOC, and I reminded him his PC (it <i>has</i> been a year and a half since the last game) refused to participate in the attack on the Castle of Shadows, is of Montano's lineage, and was an outspoken <i>opponent</i> of the act and Gratiano's lineage: it only makes sense that of all vampires, Dragomir would reach out to him.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra decided he didn't care enough about the Tzimisce's internal politics to do anything other than trade the information from the Libram Terram for boons, thereby keeping the PC's out of the act of [Tzimisce]'s &quot;diablerie&quot; entirely.<br /> <br /> ...except for the Gangrel prince PC, who went alone to Sernog monastery. There, he quietly followed the Anarchs down into the catacombs, to [Tzimisce]'s supposed resting place. He killed Lugoj, &quot;diablerized&quot; the Antediluvian, and fleshcrafted himself to look like Lugoj with no other vampire the wiser...except Lambach, who saw the whole thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T02:18:47-07:00","id":1455425,"title":"","content":"&quot;It was him! The [Gangrel Prince] not Lugoj!&quot; &quot;Shut up, Lambach.&quot; Poor guy never gets a break. . . So does the coterie get another level of clan enmity? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the update!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4712-anarade-relle","name":"Anarade Relle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T08:49:02-07:00","id":1455576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anarade Relle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455108-tc-part-16-it-s-like-someone-detonated-a-goulash-in-here?p=1455425#post1455425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It was him! The [Gangrel Prince] not Lugoj!&quot; &quot;Shut up, Lambach.&quot; Poor guy never gets a break. . . So does the coterie get another level of clan enmity? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the update!</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem.<br /> <br /> There's...significantly more going on with Lambach in my chronicle than meets the eye. For one thing, I'm going with the bit from the revised splatbook bit that &quot;Lambach&quot; is an alternate identity of<i> the</i> Lord Ruthven -- most of the off-stage events that had heavy implications for the PC coterie early on were engineered by Ruthven. It's just the case the PC's have been far, <i>far</i> below the scope of Ruthven's radar...until now.<br /> <br /> The PC's are still of use to [Tzimisce], but they've served their purpose for now. Which means they now get to deal with the consequences of the Antediluvian's direct interference. The next story is going to be an absolute shitshow because they've just about managed to piss everyone off, with few real lifelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}